# {{ title }}

%% Author note: update the version in front matter before each release. This line never renders. %%

Welcome to **{{ product }} {{ version }}**.
This line appears on its own line, because pressing Enter starts a new line.

A blank line starts a new paragraph, just like in Markdown.

::toc{depth=2}

## Text formatting

You can write *italic*, **bold**, ***bold italic***, ++underline++, ~~strikethrough~~ and ==highlighted== text.
Chemistry and math work inline: H_{2}O, x^{2} and 10^-3. ~Single tildes~ strike text, as on GitHub.
Underscores inside words are literal, so snake_case and my_variable_name are safe without escaping.
Spacing protects you too: 2 * 3 * 4 = 24, and C++ is not underlined.
**Bold**right next to text works as expected.

Style any phrase with a span: [this is red]{color=red}, [this is muted]{.muted}.
Press :kbd[Ctrl+S] to save. :abbr[YAMD]{title="Yet Another Markdown"} keeps it simple.

<b>Safe HTML</b> renders as on GitHub; scripts and event handlers are removed. Comparisons like a < b and x > y need no escaping.
Prices like $5 and $10 are not math, but $E = mc^2$ is.

## Lists

### Bullets

- Use `-`, `*` or `+`
- and keep the same marker
- for the whole list
  - Nest by indenting under the text
      - deeper still
- [x] Write the spec
- [ ] Build the parser

### Numbered steps

1. Install the CLI:

   ```bash {title="terminal"}
   npm install -g nimbus-cli
   ```

2. Numbering continues after the code block.
   This line is part of step 2.
3. Log in:
   > Tip: use your work email.
4. Done!

Only a list starting at 1 can interrupt a paragraph, so a year at the start of a line stays text:
2024. Great year.

{start=5}
5. A list that intentionally starts at five
6. and keeps counting

