## Math

The cost grows with the number of nodes $n$:

$$ {#eq:cost}
C(n) = \sum_{i=1}^{n} \frac{1}{i^2}
$$

[@eq:cost] converges as $n$ grows.

## Footnotes and citations

{{ product }} uses a consistent-hashing scheme[^hash] for storage.
Replication is configurable.^[The default is three replicas.]
The design follows earlier work on distributed systems [@lamport1978; @dean2008, p. 4].

[^hash]: Consistent hashing spreads keys across nodes.
    Adding a node only moves a small share of keys.

