## Study features

YAMD has a built-in set of tools for students and academic writers. Run **YAMD: Open Study Dashboard** to see your upcoming deadlines and study heatmap.

| Feature | How to use it |
| ------- | ------------- |
| Study-aid blocks | `:::definition`, `:::theorem`, `:::proof`, etc. |
| Flashcards | `:::card` (short Q&A included), `:cloze[answer]` |
| Quiz mode | **YAMD: Toggle Quiz Mode** — hides cloze answers |
| Review sessions | **YAMD: Review Flashcards** — SM-2 spaced repetition |
| Deadlines | `due: YYYY-MM-DD` in front matter, or `{due=…}` on tasks |
| Focus timer | **YAMD: Start Study Timer** |
| Citations | `bibliography: refs.bib` + `[@key]` |
| Export | **YAMD: Export as HTML / PDF / Word / Slides** |
| Import | **YAMD: Import Notes from Folder…** (Obsidian, Notion, HTML) |

See [examples/07-study/](07-study/README.yamd) for the complete guide.

## Escaping

Use a backslash for any literal symbol: \*not italic\*, \# not a heading, \{{ not a variable }}, \:::not a directive.

